      "content": "#include \"knn.h\"\n#include <arm_neon.h>\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * restrict groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    char * labels = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * k);\n    float * distances = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * k);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        labels[i] = -1;\n        distances[i] = -1.0f;\n    }\n\n    const float eval_x = to_evaluate.x;\n    const float eval_y = to_evaluate.y;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        Group g = groups[i];\n        Point * restrict pts = g.points;\n        int len = g.length;\n        char lab = g.label;\n\n        // Process in batches of 4 using NEON\n        int j = 0;\n        for (; j + 3 < len; j += 4) {\n            __builtin_prefetch(&pts[j+4], 0, 1);\n\n            float32x4x2_t vec = vld2q_f32((const float32_t *)&pts[j]);\n            // vec.val[0] contains x coordinates of points j..j+3\n            // vec.val[1] contains y coordinates\n\n            float32x4_t dx = vsubq_f32(vec.val[0], vdupq_n_f32(eval_x));\n            float32x4_t dy = vsubq_f32(vec.val[1], vdupq_n_f32(eval_y));\n            float32x4_t sq = vaddq_f32(vmulq_f32(dx, dx), vmulq_f32(dy, dy));\n\n            // Store to local array for insertion\n            float dists[4];\n            vst1q_f32(dists, sq);\n\n            for (int idx = 0; idx < 4; idx++) {\n                float d = dists[idx];\n                int x;\n                for (x = 0; x < k; x++) {\n                    if (d < distances[x] || distances[x] == -1.0f) {\n                        // Shift elements right from x to k-1\n                        for (int y = k - 1; y > x; y--) {\n                            distances[y] = distances[y - 1];\n                            labels[y] = labels[y - 1];\n                        }\n                        distances[x] = d;\n                        labels[x] = lab;\n                        break;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Scalar remainder\n        for (; j < len; j++) {\n            float dx = pts[j].x - eval_x;\n            float dy = pts[j].y - eval_y;\n            float d = dx*dx + dy*dy;\n\n            int x;\n            for (x = 0; x < k; x++) {\n                if (d < distances[x] || distances[x] == -1.0f) {\n                    for (int y = k - 1; y > x; y--) {\n                        distances[y] = distances[y - 1];\n                        labels[y] = labels[y - 1];\n                    }\n                    distances[x] = d;\n                    labels[x] = lab;\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    qsort(labels, k, sizeof(char), compare_for_sort);\n\n    char most_frequent = labels[0];\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\n    int current_frequency = 1;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i < k; i++) {\n        if (labels[i] != labels[i - 1]) {\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n                most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n            }\n\n            current_frequency = 1;\n        } else {\n            current_frequency++;\n        }\n\n        if (i == k - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n            most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n        }\n    }\n\n    free(labels);\n    free(distances);\n\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n    \n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n}\n",
      "path": "src/knn.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Using NEON intrinsics to compute squared Euclidean distances for batches of four points simultaneously (via vld2q_f32 deinterleave) reduces instruction count and improves SIMD throughput. Adding __builtin_prefetch hides memory latency, while restrict qualifiers on pointer parameters enable better compiler optimization. The insertion logic remains scalar but benefits from reduced distance computation overhead.",
  "notes": "Changed only src/knn.c: added NEON batch processing for groups of 4 points, prefetching, and restrict qualifiers. No changes to knn.h or other files.",
